  "notes": "Often appears in news and literary contexts describing scenes where someone is being physically or verbally restrained.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {制止|せいし}する (to restrain, to stop someone)\n- {制止|せいし}を{振|ふ}り{切|き}る (to shake off restraint)\n- {制止|せいし}を{無視|むし}する (to ignore attempts to stop one)\n- {制止|せいし}も{聞|き}かず (ignoring attempts to stop one)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {制止|せいし} — stopping someone from acting (physical/verbal intervention)\n- {抑制|よくせい} — suppression, restraint (broader; includes self-restraint and systemic controls)",
